From ef433150315726c8accd5155c0562719d0fabd95 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Raimondas Lencevicius <59739769+raimondasl@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 1 Oct 2026 12:38:45 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 16/18] Never drop oldest turns when manual_rolling summarizes

With harness summary compaction configured, manual_rolling still ran
_trim_to_fit_context before every action request, so the oldest
user/assistant pair was dropped whenever the transcript's character
estimate passed MAX_CONTEXT_LENGTH. With MAX_CONTEXT_LENGTH at the
provider's context capacity this was meant as a backstop, but it fired
before the summary trigger whenever the provider reported no usage, or
fewer tokens per character than trigger_tokens / MAX_CONTEXT_LENGTH
(about 0.17 for the Gemini profiles). A rolling-summary run could then
lose history under two policies, while continuous_conversation never
trims locally.

_request_with_retries now skips _trim_to_fit_context when a rolling
summary adapter is configured. History is lost only by summarizing: at
the usage trigger, or when the provider rejects an action request as too
long (once per action request; a second overflow fails the run), as in
continuous_conversation. manual_rolling without compaction still trims.
run_meta.json keeps runtime.context_trims, which now stays 0.

Tests: the rolling-summary profiles keep every turn with usage
unreported, at about 0.03-0.1 provider tokens per character, and with a
tiny chars-per-token estimate, including past the checked-in profiles'
1,048,576-character limit; the Standard profile still drops its oldest
turns in the same runs; and without usage only a provider overflow
compacts, with notes-off equal to the Provider Adapter without thought
steps.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
